	(text "reverse polaity:\nThe body diode is reverse-biased, so it blocks current.\nThe gate ends up above the source, so the FET stays off.\nNothing reaches the LDO."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 52.578 95.504 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "11f70bcf-5842-4ff0-8208-adb1c81bece2")
	)
	(text "Needed to stabilize the internal reference, \nwhich sets the 3.3 V output. \nThe datasheet gives a 0.7 µF minimum \n(Table 2) and recommends 1 µF. \nTwo 470 nF caps give 0.94 µF, \nabove the minimum and close to the \nrecommended value, and since they're \nC0G, that holds at 77 K. Meeting it \ncosts just one extra cap. REF_SENSE ties to REF."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 112.014 93.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "21d08437-f159-4e66-830d-df3def615fde")
	)
	(text "Power In\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 42.164 50.292 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "35a899db-b146-4da7-9cf4-676a0b0967f4")
	)
	(text "For vreg, leaving it unfiltered can hurt stability\nThe datasheet recommends 10 µF, but I reduced it \nfor the same reason as VIN and VOUT."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 239.268 91.948 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "48720a2d-9550-4f77-900a-578527e602a6")
	)
	(text "I was thinking about adding this \nfor noise filtering on the reference \nbuffer, though we may not need it \nsince noise isn't critical here. \nThe datasheet also lists it as \nnecessary (0.1 µF minimum) and \nuses it to set the soft-start, \nso I've kept it in for now. \n\nQ: Should we keep it or remove it?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170.942 123.952 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "cc5cb0b5-8319-461d-b1ba-9e2ff451d778")
	)
	(text "3v3 Regulator\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 173.482 49.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e35ef4e9-14c4-499f-8cbd-f8eb12d54db2")
	)
